  "worked_solution": "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 2 & 4 & 4\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 10 & 20\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :=\\frac{1}{10}{R}_{2} \\\\  & \u223c[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned} & x-3y=-8 \\\\  & y=2,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The final equation $y=2$ tells us the value of $y.$ Substituting this value into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\nx-3(2)=-8\\,\u21d2\\,x=-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=-2$ and $y=2.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
